The answer to the first question is No. The chain rule formula given in (3.33) cannot be used in a continuous-time stochastic environment. In fact, by "stochastic calculus," we mean a set of methods that yield the formulas equivalent to the chain rule and that approximate the laws of motion of random variables in continuous time.

