where \(R\left(x,x_{0}\right)\) represents all the remaining terms of the Taylor series expansion. Note that this remainder is made of three types of terms: partial derivatives of \(f(x)\) of order higher than 3, factorials of order higher than 3, and powers of \(\left(x-x_{0}\right)\) higher than 3.

