### 11.1 Introduction

The concept of a stochastic differential equation (SDE) was introduced in Chapter 7. In Chapter 9 we used the Ito integral to formalize this concept. The notation

\[dS_{t}=a\left(S_{t},t\right)dt+\sigma\left(S_{t},t\right)dW_{t},\quad t\in[0,\infty) \tag{11.1}\]

was justified as a symbolic way of writing

\[\int_{t}^{t+h}dS_{u}=\int_{t}^{t+h}a\left(S_{u},u\right)du+\int_{t}^{t+h} \sigma\left(S_{u},u\right)dW_{u} \tag{11.2}\]

when \(h\) is infinitesimal.

We repeat some aspects of this derivation. First of all, no concept from financial markets or financial theory was used to obtain (11.1). The basic tools used were the Ito integral and the ability

