First, some heuristics. The expected value of \(Z_{t}\) is one. By multiplying this process by the indicator function \(1_{A}\), we are in fact "zeroing out" the values assumed by \(Z_{t}\), other than those that fall in the set \(A\). Also recall that \(Z_{t}\) cannot be negative. Thus we must have:

