### 14.9 References

Transforming stochastic processes into martingales through the use of the Girsanov theorem is a deeper topic in stochastic calculus. The sources that provide the technical background of this method will all be at an advanced level. Karatzas and Shreve (1991) provides one of the more intuitive discussions. Liptser and Shiryayev (1977) is a comprehensive reference.

